From 467ded1cc294dc657061e8b817d36dfc52f950bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:01:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tar: a hardlink target must not pass through a symlink either

Hardlinks are always created at the end, by create_links_from_list(),
after the symlinks that were deferred because their target is absolute
or contains "..". The Symlink+Hardlink fix made sure that the directory
components of the link name are real directories, but link() resolves
the target the same way: an archive with

	evil -> /storage/outside     (deferred symlink)
	pulled  hardlink to evil/secret

creates evil first, and then pulled as a hardlink to
/storage/outside/secret, a file outside the extraction directory. A
later extraction that writes through existing files (tar --overwrite,
or another extractor) can then change that file. This is
CVE-2026-124745 (CNA Red Hat, 2026-11-11), for which there is no
BusyBox fix yet.

Apply the same check to the directory components of a hardlink's
target. The last component is not checked, so a hardlink to a symlink
of the archive (the "hardlink to symlink" case above) still works.
cpio uses the same function, so its hardlinks get the same check.
---
 archival/libarchive/unsafe_symlink_target.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/archival/libarchive/unsafe_symlink_target.c b/archival/libarchive/unsafe_symlink_target.c
index 65c782b..4f76401 100644
--- a/archival/libarchive/unsafe_symlink_target.c
+++ b/archival/libarchive/unsafe_symlink_target.c
@@ -63,7 +63,11 @@ void FAST_FUNC create_links_from_list(llist_t *list)
 		// SYMLINK_OUTSIDE_EXTRACT_DIR/etc/passwd sort of thing.
 		// (Our delayed creation of symlinks is not defending against it,
 		// we could create SYMLINK_OUTSIDE_EXTRACT_DIR ourself!)
-		if (!all_dir_components_are_dirs(linkname)) {
+		// The target of a hardlink is resolved the same way by link():
+		// SYMLINK_OUTSIDE_EXTRACT_DIR/secret would pull an outside file in.
+		if (!all_dir_components_are_dirs(linkname)
+		 || (list->data[0] && !all_dir_components_are_dirs(target))
+		) {
 			errno = ENOTDIR;
 			goto err;
 		}
